    "result_text": "All changes are complete and the test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `bulkSignupWarning` rule for `POST /api/owners`: when more than 80 owners have already been created on the request's (adjusted) business day, the created/returned owner carries `bulkSignupWarning: true`, otherwise `false`.\n\nFollowing the existing `namesakeCount` pattern (a value captured at creation time and stored on the entity), the changes are:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only boolean `bulkSignupWarning` property to the `Owner` schema (generates the DTO field).\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added the `bulkSignupWarning` field (`@Column(name = \"bulk_signup_warning\")`) with getter/setter.\n3. **Schema SQL** (h2, hsqldb, postgres, mysql) \u2014 added a `bulk_signup_warning BOOLEAN` column to the `owners` table.\n4. **`FlagBulkSignup.java`** (new function) \u2014 runs before `SaveOwner`, counts existing owners registered on this owner's business day (mirroring `EnsureDailyOwnerLimit`'s per-day accumulation), and sets the flag when the count exceeds the threshold of 80.\n5. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired a `flagBulkSignup` step (under `transaction` governance) between `countNamesakes` and `save`.\n\nThe MapStruct `OwnerMapper` maps the field automatically by name, so `GET /api/owners/{id}` returns the stored value \u2014 which is what the acceptance test asserts (`$.bulkSignupWarning == false` for a fresh single create). The `>80` branch shares the same per-day counting path.",
